course: dictionary
lesson: 2105
title: When things do not match
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To contradict someone is to say the opposite of what they said, because you think they are wrong. Two facts that contradict each other cannot both be true. «Every answer she gives, the Caterpillar contradicts in a few rude words.» The Caterpillar does not agree with Alice. It says the opposite each time, so the words do not match.
explain: Look for the clue. «When two stories contradict each other and there is no proof, the honest answer is «we don't know».» Two stories that do not match cannot both be true, so you cannot yet be sure which one is right.
explain: You can also contradict yourself. That means saying two things that do not fit together. Careful speakers and writers avoid this. Polite disagreement is fine, but contradicting an adult rudely is not kind.
fact: Contradict means to say the opposite of what someone has said, to show they are wrong.
fact: The forms are contradict, contradicts, contradicted and contradicting, as in «she contradicts him» or «they contradicted each other».
fact: If two facts contradict each other, they cannot both be true.
fact: In science, a result that contradicts your prediction shows that your prediction was wrong.
fact: To contradict yourself is to say two things that do not fit together, and «don't contradict me» is a way of telling someone to stop arguing.
exercise: Sam says the sky is green. Mia says, «No, the sky is blue.» What is Mia doing? | *Contradicting Sam, saying the opposite | Singing a song | Going to sleep | Agreeing with Sam
exercise: «The two maps contradict each other, so only one of them can be right.» What does contradict mean here? | Are drawn in colour | Are very old | *Are the opposite of each other, so they cannot both be true | Are the same, so they are both right
exercise: Which sentence shows someone contradicting themselves? | *I love cake, and I never want to eat cake. | Cake is sweet and round. | We baked a cake on Friday. | I like cake, and I had a slice today.
test: «The Caterpillar contradicts every answer Alice gives.» What does the Caterpillar do? | Agrees with every answer | *Says the opposite of what Alice says | Tells Alice a joke | Falls asleep
test: Ben says, «The shop is open on Sunday.» Ella says, «It is not open, it is shut.» What is Ella doing? | Agreeing with Ben | *Contradicting Ben, saying the opposite | Shouting at Ben | Asking Ben for help
exam: Two stories contradict each other and there is no proof, so what is the honest answer? | The loudest one wins | The first story is always right | Both must be true | *We don't know
